# Parcego Courier Platform – Courier Dashboard Rule

## Objective

Build the **Courier Dashboard UI** for the Parcego Courier Business Platform, strictly following the provided user flowchart and naming/scoping conventions.  
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (for client-side state, if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)
- **Naming & Scoping:**  
  - All HTML IDs and class names must strictly follow the rules in `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`:
    - IDs: `parcego-[component]-[purpose]-[unique-identifier]`
    - Classes: `parcego-[block]__[element]--[modifier]` (BEM/SMACSS, always prefixed by `parcego`)
    - Dynamic elements: Append a unique hash/UUID for runtime-generated IDs/classes

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Dashboard Features (All UI, No Backend)
- **Welcome Banner:** Personalized greeting, courier name, and quick stats (e.g., deliveries today, completed, earnings)
- **Quick Actions:** Prominent buttons for "Start Next Delivery", "View Route", "Performance Stats"
- **Assigned Deliveries:** List or cards of today's assigned deliveries (mock data), with status badges and action buttons (e.g., "Scan Package", "Start Route", "Mark Delivered")
- **Delivery Workflow:**  
  - **Scan Package:** Barcode/QR scanner UI (mock)
  - **Route Navigation:** Map placeholder with route steps (mock)
  - **Proof of Delivery:** Photo upload UI, digital signature (mock)
  - **Mark as Delivered:** Confirmation UI
- **Performance Tracking:** Mini chart or summary cards (mock data)
- **Notifications:** Section for recent alerts or updates (mock)
- **Navigation:** Bottom nav or sidebar for dashboard sections (Deliveries, Route, Performance, Profile)
- **Profile/Account Menu:** Avatar with dropdown for account settings and logout (UI only)
- **Mobile-First:** Layout and interactions must be optimized for mobile and tablet use

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for all navigation.
- All flows must match the provided user flowchart.
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for lists, workflow steps, and status updates.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.
- **All IDs and class names must strictly follow `@naming-and-scoping.mdc` for easy inspection and debugging.**

---

## 6. Deliverables

- Courier Dashboard page and all required UI components.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the courier dashboard demo.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards, especially `@naming-and-scoping.mdc`.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Courier Dashboard UI for the Parcego platform, ready for future backend/API integration and mobile-first usage.

---

**Brand Note:**  
All new code, files, and identifiers must use the **Parcego** brand name and updated naming structure.